// Package tachyonsdk is the official Go SDK bindings for Tachyon Mesh FaaS guests.
//
// The gen/ subdirectory holds real Component Model guest bindings for the
// kv-consumer world, generated by wit-bindgen-go (go.bytecodealliance.org)
// from wit/tachyon.wit (a vendored, byte-for-byte copy of sdk/wit/tachyon.wit,
// kept in sync by scripts/check_wit_sdk_sync.sh -- cargo/npm-style packaging
// isn't a concept for a Go module, but the same "generate from a vendored
// local copy, not a path escaping this directory" reasoning applies).
//
// Regenerate after any kv-partition WIT change with:
//
//	go run go.bytecodealliance.org/cmd/wit-bindgen-go@v0.7.0 generate -w kv-consumer -o gen -p github.com/astorise/Tachyon-Mesh/sdk/go/gen wit
//
// Building a real guest component from Go requires TinyGo (mainline Go's
// gc compiler does not support the Component Model ABI that wit-bindgen-go
// emits -- see the go:wasmimport parameter-type restrictions in
// https://pkg.go.dev/cmd/compile for why `go build -target=wasip1` alone
// rejects the generated gen/tachyon/mesh/kv-partition package):
//
// Compose a WIT world with wasi:cli/command, kv-partition and the Tachyon
// handler, then pass it via -wit-package and -wit-world. The repository's
// tests/sdk-wasm/build-and-test.sh demonstrates the complete working build.
package tachyonsdk

//go:generate go run go.bytecodealliance.org/cmd/wit-bindgen-go@v0.7.0 generate -w kv-consumer -o gen -p github.com/astorise/Tachyon-Mesh/sdk/go/gen wit
